==English==

===Etymology===
From {{bor|en|as|মুঢ়া}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A [[stool]] made of woven [[cane]], used in northeast India.
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2000|author=Sanjoy Hazarika|title=Rites of Passage
|passage=Keramat brought out a '''''murha''''', a low stool made of woven cane. He squatted on the earth beside me.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2010|author={{w|Jahnavi Barua}}|title=Rebirth|page=154|publisher=Penguin
|passage=There is only a '''murha''' in the opposite corner and I do not want to be uncomfortable now. I lower myself into my father's chair.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2011|author={{w|Arupa Patangia Kalita}}|translator=Deepika Phukan|title=The Story of Felanee
|passage=She had recently learned to make cane '''murhas''' and now, every evening, when she returned from the market, she would first finish her cooking and then make '''murhas''' while Moni finished his studies.}}

